{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "06YV", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : (\\Sh(\\mathcal{C}), \\mathcal{O}) \\to (\\Sh(\\mathcal{D}), \\mathcal{O}')$", "MATH_0002": "$$\nLf^*(\n\\mathcal{F}^\\bullet \\otimes_{\\mathcal{O}'}^{\\mathbf{L}} \\mathcal{G}^\\bullet\n) =\nLf^*\\mathcal{F}^\\bullet \n\\otimes_{\\mathcal{O}}^{\\mathbf{L}}\nLf^*\\mathcal{G}^\\bullet \n$$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{F}^\\bullet, \\mathcal{G}^\\bullet \\in \\Ob(D(\\mathcal{O}'))$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-pullback-tensor-product}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:78752eb0bcd3c91771698ca622e76ba686db7b8c67ef869cd7db934eebf0512e", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:10d54c7958fb08edf736d89d8130a9335b682c10ca05c9685ccc0b2c13a3eea4", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001>\nbe a morphism of ringed topoi.\nThere is a canonical bifunctorial isomorphism\n<MATH_0002>\nfor <MATH_0003>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:866fd8d816a430a830a8817d700a66caa362a4697f8ee904c3ec6f494d2fb26e", "unit_id": "tag:07A4:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "06YV", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{F}^\\bullet$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{G}^\\bullet$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{O}'$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{F}^\\bullet \\otimes_{\\mathcal{O}'}^{\\mathbf{L}} \\mathcal{G}^\\bullet$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{F}^\\bullet \\otimes_{\\mathcal{O}'} \\mathcal{G}^\\bullet$", "MATH_0006": "$\\text{Tot}(\\mathcal{F}^\\bullet \\otimes_{\\mathcal{O}'} \\mathcal{G}^\\bullet)$", "MATH_0007": "$$\n\\text{Tot}(f^*\\mathcal{F}^\\bullet \\otimes_{\\mathcal{O}}\nf^*\\mathcal{G}^\\bullet)\n\\longrightarrow\nf^*\\text{Tot}(\\mathcal{F}^\\bullet \\otimes_{\\mathcal{O}'} \\mathcal{G}^\\bullet)\n$$", "MATH_0008": "$f^*\\mathcal{F}^p \\otimes_{\\mathcal{O}} f^*\\mathcal{G}^q \\to\nf^*(\\mathcal{F}^p \\otimes_{\\mathcal{O}'} \\mathcal{G}^q)$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-derived-base-change}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-K-flat-resolution}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-tensor-product-K-flat}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{sites-modules-lemma-tensor-flats}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{sites-modules-lemma-tensor-product-pullback}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:bc496f6dc8feff3f35c37c0b2ad7319e8e084239854b3b9507726f0e7baa401a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:f7a81424b455592882fec126fdb8663fd1b93cd9ad648911e9b74801e5457623", "source_text": "By our construction of derived pullback in\nLemma <REF_0001>.\nand the existence of resolutions in\nLemma <REF_0002>\nwe may replace <MATH_0001> and <MATH_0002>\nby complexes of <MATH_0003>-modules which are K-flat and have\nflat terms. In this case\n<MATH_0004>\nis just the total complex associated to the double complex\n<MATH_0005>.\nThe complex\n<MATH_0006>\nis K-flat with flat terms by Lemma <REF_0003> and\nModules on Sites, Lemma <REF_0004>.\nHence the isomorphism of the lemma comes from the isomorphism\n<MATH_0007>\nwhose constituents are the isomorphisms\n<MATH_0008> of\nModules on Sites, Lemma <REF_0005>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d7a993f53d5fa13cfe3fb05eae0aae8dc467041802a3cfe5dd4f6187c9bac41f", "unit_id": "tag:07A4:proof"}
